The calculates_results_stats() function uses the information in the results dictionary to calculate the final statistics.

The following counts are calculated:

Number of images
Number of dog images
Number of not-a-dog images
Number of correctly classified dog images
Number of correctly classified not-a-dog images
Number of correctly classified dog breeds

The calculations are based on the values stored at indexes 2, 3, and 4 of the results dictionary.

Number of Images

The number of images is the length of the results dictionary:

n_images = len(results_dic)
Number of Dog Images

A pet image is a dog when:

results_dic[key][3] == 1
Number of Not-a-Dog Images

A pet image is not a dog when:

results_dic[key][3] == 0
Correctly Classified Dog Images

A dog is correctly classified when:

results_dic[key][3] == 1 and results_dic[key][4] == 1
Correctly Classified Not-a-Dog Images

A non-dog is correctly classified when:

results_dic[key][3] == 0 and results_dic[key][4] == 0
Correctly Classified Dog Breeds

A breed is correctly classified when the image is a dog and the labels match:

results_dic[key][3] == 1 and results_dic[key][2] == 1

The required percentages are calculated using the following formulas:

Correctly Classified Dogs =
(correct dog classifications / number of dog images) × 100

Correctly Classified Not-a-Dogs =
(correct non-dog classifications / number of non-dog images) × 100

Correctly Classified Dog Breeds =
(correct breed classifications / number of dog images) × 100

A conditional check is used when calculating the percentage of non-dog images so that division by zero is avoided.
